# UC-012 · AI

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-012-classify-support-ticket/`. Owner: `ai-architect`.
> Inherits the ports, their domain types and the review state from `10-domain.md`, the trigger's
> deadline from `30-rest.md` or `25-messaging.md` — doesn't redecide them. Contains no code. Form
> references in `.claude/skills/ai-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/ai.md`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Mother spec | `00-use-case.md` |
| Why this partial exists | `10-domain.md` § Ports: `TicketClassifier`, kind `LLM` |
| AI package | `adapter.out.ai` (blueprint `packages.map`) |
| Spring AI line | 2.x — the project runs Boot 4 (`pom.xml` parent); BOM resolved by the Initializr on write, never written here |
| Divergences from other partials | none |

## 1 · AI ports

| Port (method) | Kind | Asks | Returns | "Could not decide" value | Review state it leads to |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `TicketClassifier.suggest(TicketText)` | `LLM` | a category and a priority for the ticket text | `ClassificationSuggestion` — `Suggested(category, priority)` or `Undecided(reason)` | `Undecided` | `Ticket.status = AWAITING_TRIAGE` (`10-domain.md` § Invariants) |

The model suggests; `Ticket.applySuggestion` decides. A `CRITICAL` priority is never a suggestion:
the domain rule "an outage keyword from an enterprise customer" sets it (`10-domain.md`).

## 2 · Provider and models

| Decision | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Provider | OpenAI, `spring-ai-starter-model-openai` | Asked: the company's contract and data-processing agreement are with it |
| Model per port | `ticket-classifier`: `gpt-4.1-mini`, temperature 0.0, max 200 output tokens | Asked; non-reasoning, so temperature is accepted. A classification wants the most likely label |
| Inherited? | no — first AI port of this project | `pom.xml` carries no Spring AI dependency |

## 3 · Prompts and output

| Port | Prompt resources | Variables | Answer type | Closed fields | Unreadable answer |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ticket-classifier` | `prompts/ticket-classifier-system.st`, `prompts/ticket-classifier-user.st` | `ticket` — inside the `TICKET START` / `TICKET END` markers the system prompt names as data | `TicketClassificationAnswer(TicketCategory category, TicketPriority priority)`, declared in the adapter | both enums; `null` category = none fits | `Undecided` — malformed, outside the enum, empty, refused, `null`, or `CRITICAL` |

Schema validation on (`validateSchema()`): one non-matching answer goes back to the model with the
error before the adapter sees it. Template delimiters `<` `>`: the system prompt shows a JSON example.

## 4 · Data sent

`@.claude/rules/personal-data.md` § In transit — asked per field, before the prompt was written.

| Field available | Sent | Form | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Ticket.text` | yes | full | the classification's whole input |
| `Ticket.customerEmail` | no | — | not needed to classify |
| `Ticket.customerName` | no | — | not needed to classify |
| `Ticket.accountId` | no | — | not needed to classify |

Receiver: the model provider, outside the project, under the company's data-processing agreement
(recorded by the user on 2026-10-12). Customers do write personal data into the text itself; that is
accepted under the same agreement and recorded here — masking inside free text is not part of this
case.

## 5 · Vector store

none — no port of kind `vector store`.

## 6 · Failure and retry

| Port | Timeout (per attempt) | Retrying layer | Attempts | Trigger's own retry |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ticket-classifier` | 4 s — under the 5 s deadline of `POST /tickets` (`30-rest.md` § 2); p99.9 measured at 2.8 s | the OpenAI SDK (`spring.ai.openai.max-retries: 1`) | 2 | none — a REST request |

| Failure | Family | `errorCode` | Reaches our caller as |
|---|---|---|---|
| 429, 503 | dependency unavailable | `TICKET_CLASSIFIER_MODEL_UNAVAILABLE` | the ticket is created `AWAITING_TRIAGE` — the use case catches it: classification is best effort (`00-use-case.md` § Alternative flows) |
| read timeout, connection lost, 502, 504 | outcome unknown | `TICKET_CLASSIFIER_MODEL_NO_ANSWER` | same |
| any other 4xx/5xx | dependency response | `TICKET_CLASSIFIER_MODEL_FAILED` | same, and the `ai.review.share` alarm |

| Project-wide piece | NEW or REUSE |
|---|---|
| `AiProperties`, `AiClientConfig`, `AiFailureTranslator` | NEW |
| Integration families (`IntegrationException` and its three subclasses) | REUSE — `28-http-client.md` of UC-004 created them |

## 7 · Observability

| Metric | Alarm it exists for |
|---|---|
| `gen_ai.client.operation` (tags `gen_ai.request.model`, `error.type`) — from the library's observations | p99 above 3.5 s for 15 min: the timeout is about to cut answers |
| `gen_ai.client.token.usage` (tag `gen_ai.token.type`) | daily input tokens 50 % above the 7-day average: a prompt or an input grew |
| `ai.review.share` (tag `port`) — counted by the use case on `Undecided` | above 20 % for 1 h: the prompt, the model or the input changed |

Content logging: every flag false (`application-ai.yml.example`).

## 8 · Test cases

| Level | Case | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| Contract (stub `ChatModel`) | valid answer | `Suggested(BILLING, NORMAL)` |
| Contract | category outside the enum | `Undecided`, after the schema retry |
| Contract | malformed answer | `Undecided` |
| Contract | `null` category | `Undecided` |
| Contract | `CRITICAL` priority | `Undecided` |
| Contract | prompt content | the ticket inside its markers; no e-mail, name or account id |
| Contract | SDK rate limit | dependency unavailable, `TICKET_CLASSIFIER_MODEL_UNAVAILABLE`, wait carried |
| Provider IT (WireMock) | happy path | mapped; request names the port's model, the key header and the ticket |
| Provider IT | 503 | dependency unavailable after exactly 2 requests |
| Provider IT | 429 + `Retry-After` | dependency unavailable, wait carried |
| Provider IT | delay above the timeout | outcome unknown after exactly 2 requests |
| Provider IT | 400 | dependency response after exactly 1 request |

