## 12 · Deferred

none

## Compose services

none — a chat model is a remote API, never a container of this project.

## Design patterns

| Force or symptom | Pattern | Classes and interfaces it creates | "When not" checked |
|---|---|---|---|
| The port must not know a model answers it, and the provider SDK's types must stop at the adapter | Adapter | `ChatTicketClassifier implements TicketClassifier`, `TicketClassificationAnswer` | Not a Strategy over providers: one provider, chosen in § 2 |

One row per pattern this layer adopts, decided through
`@.claude/skills/gof-design-patterns/SKILL.md` § Design-time use. Consolidation collects this
section into `UC-NNN-spec.md`.

## Impact on approved use cases

none

## Implementation order

1. The dependencies of § 10
2. `AiProperties`, `AiClientConfig`, `AiFailureTranslator` in the AI package — once per project
3. The prompt resources of § 3
4. `TicketClassificationAnswer` and `ChatTicketClassifier` — after `TicketClassifier` and the domain types exist
5. Properties in `application.yml`
6. Tests — `40-tests.md`: every row of § 8
